1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
I need help!
我需要帮助！

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,690
I have to fix a leaking pipe in my bathroom but I’m not sure where to begin.
我得修理浴室里漏水的的水管，但我不确定从哪里开始。

3
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:18,230
I know I lack the necessary DIY skills, but luckily there are numerous books and online videos that will hopefully give me the information I need.
我知道我缺乏必要的自己动手的技能，但幸运的是，有许多的书籍和在线视频，有望给我提供我需要的信息。

4
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:29,810
Publications that help us to help ourselves are nothing new, but the range of them is increasing with advice being given far beyond practical tasks around the house.
帮助我们自助的出版物并不是什么新鲜事，但这类出版物的范围在不断扩大，所提供的建议远远超出了家庭的实用任务。

5
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:38,790
Bookshops these days are full of titles which claim to boost your self-confidence, your wealth, your love life or your career.
如今的书店里摆满了各种书籍，这些书籍的标题声称可以增强你的自信心、增加你的财富、改善你的爱情生活或提升你的职业发展。

6
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:42,330
Some claim to improve your life within seven days!
有些书甚至声称能在七天内改善你的生活！

7
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:50,140
It‘s big business and it’s thought that the self-help industry is worth $10bn in the US alone.
这可是个大生意，据说仅在美国，自助类产业的价值就高达100亿美元。

8
00:00:50,140 --> 00:01:01,680
The first self-help book called ‘How to Win Friends and Influence People‘ was published in 1936, and has since sold 30 million copies and is still popular now.
第一本自助书籍《如何赢得朋友和影响他人》于1936年出版，从那以后已经售出了3000万册，并且至今仍然很受欢迎。

9
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:07,220
It includes guidance on how to make people like you and how to make your life happier.
这本书包括了如何让别人喜欢你以及如何让你的生活更幸福的指导。

10
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:18,350
It might seem strange to think that we need a book to tell us how to live our lives but self-help books remain a go-to remedy for those of us looking for enlightenment.
想到我们需要一本书来告诉我们如何生活，这可能看起来很奇怪，但对于我们这些寻求启迪的人来说，自助书籍仍然是一种首选的解决办法。

11
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:21,860
There are, of course, trends in what we need help with.
当然，在我们需要帮助的事情上也存在一些趋势。

12
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:33,980
Emma Marshall, who works at British bookshop Waterstones, says “at the moment we’re in the tidying up, getting rid of things trend... I think the trend right now is about slowing down in your life.”
在英国水石书店工作的艾玛·马歇尔说：“目前我们正处于整理、清理东西的潮流中......我认为现在的潮流是让你的生活慢下来。”

13
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:44,860
It seems there is always something we need help with, and reading about it can be very therapeutic - it makes us feel good, even if we don‘t do anything about it.
似乎总是有一些我们需要帮助的事情，而且阅读相关内容可能是非常有疗效的——它让我们感觉良好，即使我们对此什么也不做。

14
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:49,170
Of course, the internet has become the place to go to for salvation.
当然，互联网已经成为寻求救赎的地方。

15
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:57,180
We’ve got used to searching for solutions online, and now these solutions even include how to fix or improve our lives.
我们已经习惯了在网上搜索解决方案，现在这些解决方案甚至包括如何修复或改善我们的生活。

16
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:09,600
Interestingly, psychologist Caroline Beaton, says people called ‘millennials‘ are self-critical — they are aware of their own faults — which also means they’re more likely to spend time and money on self-help.
有趣的是，心理学家卡罗琳·比顿说，被称为“千禧一代”的人很擅于自我批评——他们知道自己的缺点——这也意味着他们更有可能在自助方面花费时间和金钱。

17
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:21,030
There‘s also a theory that the self-help industry does well during a recession — people are perhaps even more likely to reach for self-help to improve their situation.
还有一种理论认为，自助类产业在经济衰退期间表现良好——人们可能更倾向于寻求自助来改善自己的处境。

18
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:28,660
Whatever the reason for the continued interest in self-help, it’s good to know help is at hand when we need it.
无论人们对自助持续感兴趣的原因是什么，知道在我们需要帮助的时候，帮助就在身边是件好事。

19
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:37,530
The alternative to finding a happier life is just to come to terms with yourself as you are - I know, I read about it in a book!
除了寻找更幸福的生活之外，另一种选择就是接受真实的自己——我知道，我在一本书里读到过！

20
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:39,880
Do you believe in self-help books?
你相信自助书籍吗？
